# Vendored third-party tool binaries/data (nmap/nuclei/ffuf/gobuster/sqlmap/...).
# These must be fetched via a setup script, NOT committed (~163MB).
# Already-tracked copies are removed from the index via `git rm -r --cached tools/`
# (working files on disk are untouched; this only stops FUTURE commits).
# Git history still contains the old blobs until a separate `git filter-repo` pass.
/tools/
!/tools/README.md
/tmp_*

# Local CTF challenge working dirs — packed/unpacked ELF binaries, libc/ld
# blobs, exploit scripts, and captured flags. These are per-challenge local
# artifacts (like loot/), NOT framework assets, and must not enter repo history.
# Solve write-ups live in agent memory; keep working files on disk only.
/challenges/
